## Execution Plan
Follow this plan step by step:
1. Locate the Mozio email confirmation template and the data-payload builder that feeds it; identify where the outbound trip promo code discount amount is computed and rendered (line-item-level discount line with label and amount).

2. In the data-payload builder, ensure the promo code discount amount is calculated for each return trip line item independently (per fromStation/toStation pair), using the same discount calculation logic as the outbound leg, and is included in the payload under the same field name/structure used for outbound line items.

3. Update the discount calculation logic so that promo applicability is evaluated per line item: apply the discount only when the promo code is valid for that leg’s date (dateFrom/dateTo) and configured to apply to that leg; return zero/omit when the promo is outbound-only, expired for the return date, or no promo exists.

4. Modify the Mozio email confirmation template to iterate over all line items (outbound and return) and render the promo discount line (label + amount) for each item that has a non-zero discount amount, using the same format, position, currency formatting, and decimal precision as the outbound trip.

5. Ensure the template omits the promo discount line for any line item whose discount amount is zero or not applicable, consistent with existing outbound zero-discount handling.

6. Add accessibility attributes/markup to the promo discount line (e.g., semantic element, aria-label or visible text for label+amount) and verify color contrast for the discount label and amount text meets WCAG AA.

7. Add unit tests for the payload builder covering: return trip with promo applied to both legs, multiple line items with different station pairs, outbound-only promo, expired promo for return date, no promo, decimal discount amounts, discount exceeding base fare, and dateFrom/dateTo spanning different calendar dates — asserting the return trip discount amount is present and correct.

8. Add template/render tests asserting: discount line renders for both legs when applicable, format/position matches outbound, discount line is omitted when zero/not applicable, no errors when no promo or outbound-only promo, and accessibility markup is present.

9. Run the full test suite and lint checks; verify no regressions in existing Mozio email confirmation rendering for outbound-only and non-promo orders.

